# Infrastructure rules

Applies to `src/Core/` and `src/Infrastructure/` (not TrayApp UI).

- Use async/await for I/O; pass `CancellationToken` through orchestrator and log store calls.
- Keep parsers and probes static and pure where possible (`BuildLogParser`, `DotNetRunOutputParser`, `LocalPortProbe`).
- Do not block the stdout callback thread with heavy work — debounce disk writes and port probes.
- Child process environment: use `DotNetProcessConfigurator` — do not duplicate env sanitization.
- Never log or persist user secrets from `%LocalAppData%` settings.
- General C# style: `.cursor/context/coding-standards.md`.
